From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: quire <quire@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:51:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] embed: js api

Feature `embed` (wasm32 only): instead of starting the page of its own, the
wasm `main` installs `globalThis.inkboardEmbed`, so that another page can show
a board inside its own interface and own the file (docs/WEB.md, "Embedding").

- `mount(canvas, options)` resolves to a handle: `snapshot`, `setBoard`,
  `revision`, `isDirty`, `markSaved`, `setTheme`, `setReadOnly`, `setName`,
  `setActive`, `focus`, `fitView`, `destroy`. One board per page: a second
  mount rejects with `start` until the first is destroyed.
- Host mode (`App::host`): no New, Open, Join, Save as, Quit, Language or
  "Present full screen" (F5 does nothing either), no board name field, no
  "Saved" label and no tab title; Ctrl/Cmd+S calls the host's `onSave`;
  `onChange` reports a new revision, or a change of the text being typed, at
  most once per frame and never in the middle of a gesture.
- `setBoard` resets the history and every transient editor state (text being
  typed, gesture, draft, dialog, presentation) before the new board shows.
- `setActive(false)` drops the periodic repaint of a hidden host page.
- `platform::init` is split: `init_ctx` (context, paste listener once per page,
  ignoring pastes while the board is not focused) and `init_page` (address and
  network listeners, the page of its own only), plus `clear_ctx`.
- A panic is reported to `onError` through a timer of the page, which still
  fires after the instance has trapped.

No new interface text: what a host page owns is hidden, not relabelled.
